{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":17655204,"ns":0,"title":"Automatic semigroup","extract":"In mathematics, an automatic semigroup is a finitely generated semigroup equipped with several regular languages over an alphabet representing a generating set. One of these languages determines \"canonical forms\" for the elements of the semigroup, the other languages determine if two canonical forms represent elements that differ by multiplication by a generator.","description":"Mathematical structure","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}